                 UX FOLLOW-UPS landed with Phase 6:

                 - Handshake loading overlay.  The 3-5s handshake
                 would otherwise let the user switch to a tab whose
                 state hasn't arrived and read it as "device has no
                 channels / no MQTT".  Notebook is now wrapped in a
                 GtkOverlay with a 64x64 centred GtkSpinner +
                 "Reading configuration from device…" label;
                 show_loading/hide_loading also flip notebook
                 sensitivity so tabs cannot be clicked while the
                 spinner is up.  drop_connection hides it too so a
                 dialog-close mid-handshake leaves no ghost widget.

                 - Channels page list height.  set_min_content_
                 height(220) + set_propagate_natural_height(TRUE)
                 + a hard set_size_request(list, -1, 200) on the
                 GtkListBox itself.  Without all three, the FALSE/
                 FALSE-packed Channels expander pinned the scrolled
                 list to a single row.  Same pattern (with smaller
                 numbers) used for the Share page's channel
                 checkbox list -- the QR area's set_size_request
                 was eating the slack the list needed.

                 - Trash-can delete glyph.  Per-row delete on the
                 Channels page uses "user-trash-symbolic" (verified
                 present in the icon theme) instead of "edit-
                 delete"; reads as "discard" rather than "erase".

                 GOTCHAS for future cousins (Phase 7 / 11+):

                 (i) ProtoBuf field numbers in pip-mesh's bash
                 docstrings were not always accurate (Phase 5
                 already hit this on set_channel: docstring 32,
                 code 33).  For Phase 6 the field numbers came
                 verbatim out of build_channel_set_hex /
                 print_qr_config and matched what the firmware
                 expects; the test pins them at the URL level so
                 a future "tidy up" cannot silently drift.

                 (ii) Region UNSET would brick the receiver on
                 full-config import (proto3 zero == UNSET, no fall-
                 back).  refresh_url skips emission in full-config
                 mode unless PnMeshState->have_lora_config is TRUE
                 (a small dim notice paints in its place) so the
                 URL/QR pair stays blank (not "garbage URL") until
                 the handshake actually surfaces a LoRa config.

                 (iii) Cairo QR render budgets four modules of
                 quiet zone around the matrix even though Meshtastic
                 phone apps are tolerant; without it the white
                 border collapses when the dialog uses a dark theme
                 and decode rate drops.  Drawing happens against
                 the cached URL so toggle->draw is one cycle of
                 queue_draw -- no re-encode on every expose.

                 (iv) GtkScrolledWindow's set_min_content_height
                 ALONE was repeatedly observed to be ignored when
                 the scrolled window lives inside a GtkExpander
                 packed FALSE/FALSE in a tab box: the listbox
                 collapsed to one row.  The reliable recipe is
                 min_content_height + propagate_natural_height +
                 an explicit gtk_widget_set_size_request on the
                 listbox itself.  Any future tab-hosted scrolled
                 list (Phase 7 test page, Phase 11+ module pages)
                 should follow the same belt-and-braces pattern.

                 (v) Long URLs in a single-line GtkEntry hide
                 their dynamic suffix behind the (identical) URL
                 prefix.  Wrapping selectable GtkLabel was the
                 right widget; reuse it for any other "show me
                 this URL" affordance instead of an entry.
