(35) Promote the recurring device-dialog UI building blocks into PUBLIC
reusable GtkWidget subclasses in libpipnode-gui, so every plugin's
Devices dialog looks and behaves uniformly.  The pipnode-zigbee-plugin
(~/pipnode-projects/pipnode-zigbee-plugin/src/pn-zigbee-gui.c -- READ
ONLY, the model, do NOT modify) builds a rich Zigbee Devices dialog on
the #34 toolkit but still HAND-ROLLS most of its higher-level controls as
private helper functions assembling raw GtkGrid rows -- e.g.
zb_add_switch_control / zb_add_int_control (labelled setting rows),
zb_make_get_button (a control with a per-row "refresh/get" icon button),
zb_add_numeric_presets (a spin paired with a preset-value combo:
"100ms/1s/10s"), the firmware + pairing status/progress sections
(state label + progress bar + action button), the modal join-window
countdown dialog (spinner + progress + time-remaining + joined-count),
read-only info blocks, and enum combos that grow an "(unknown)" fallback
entry.  None of these are reusable widgets, so each plugin re-invents
them and dialogs drift apart.  Goal: identify the common blocks (start
from the zigbee list above), and ship them as proper GtkWidget-derived
classes alongside the existing PnDeviceCombo / PnDeviceSpin /
PnInlineEditLabel (gui-tier, lib/, PUBLIC installed headers, core stays
GTK-free, no ABI bump -- new exported symbols, not PnNodeClass vfuncs),
documented in PLUGINS so plugin writers consume pipnode's widgets instead
of hand-building rows.  No sub-items / phase tracker yet -- scope to be
broken down later.

