(36) Stop ModemManager from probing Meshtastic serial devices.  When a tty
appears, ModemManager (root) opens it and fires AT commands -- which toggles
DTR/RTS (rebooting the ESP32) and races pipnode's open.  pipnode's in-use
guard is a /proc scan that can't see root-owned holders, so it misses MM.
Fix: ship a udev rule setting ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE=1 for the Meshtastic
VID:PIDs (packaging step), and/or inhibit the device over MM's D-Bus API
around open.  Caveat: 10c4:ea60 is generic CP2102 (see #33); a blanket
ignore also hides real CP2102 modems.  Touches system config -- weigh against
the minimal-invasive-packaging line.

(37) Converge the two Meshtastic serial stacks.  The Devices dialog
(pn-mesh-serial.c / pn-mesh-discover.c / pn-mesh-connection.c) and the
Meshtastic NODE (pn-meshtastic.c) -- both GTK-free core -- each carry their
OWN careful-but-divergent serial open, sysfs USB scan and 0x94 0xC3 frame
codec.  Neither is careless; they just differ, and #33/#36 would otherwise
have to be fixed twice.  Share the transport+discovery+framing layer (NOT the
whole snapshot-oriented PnMeshConnection -- the node needs a long-lived
streaming session and keeps its own loop).

  37.1 DONE Characterization tests first (hot path: live messaging).  Pin the
  node's current open / discovery / frame behaviour before touching it, per
  the tests-before-refactor rule.  tests/unit/test-pn-mesh-node.c compiles the
  node TU directly (libpipnode-core links as a .so, so the test's own copies of
  the few exported symbols win and only the static helpers are exercised; the
  GObject is never instantiated).  19 cases / 105 checks pin: the 0x94 0xC3
  frame envelope + exact ToRadio/MeshPacket/Data wire bytes for text /
  want_config / heartbeat; the varint+fixed32 protobuf primitives; the
  frame_extract accumulator (clean / split / junk / oversized-recovery, and the
  DIVERGENCE that the node DROPS a zero-length frame where the dialog reader
  yields it -- so 37.3's reconciliation is a deliberate choice); serial_open's
  flock+TIOCEXCL EBUSY exclusivity, O_CLOEXEC and raw 115200 8N1 (against a
  pseudo-terminal); and discovery -- the known_devices VID:PID:label table,
  find_tty_under's one-level + nested sysfs walk, and list_devices' sorted
  NULL-terminated /dev contract.

  37.2 DONE Unify the open into pn_mesh_serial_open as BEST-OF-BOTH: kept
  the dialog's refuse-BEFORE-open guard (pn_mesh_tty_in_use -> no DTR/RTS
  toggle on an in-use device) AND folded in the node's flock(LOCK_EX) +
  O_CLOEXEC (serial.c's open lacked both).  The node's private serial_open()
  is deleted; pn_meshtastic_read_channels() and worker_main() now open
  through pn_mesh_serial_open() and pull the raw fd via the new
  pn_mesh_serial_get_fd() accessor for their existing poll()/serial_write_all
  loops (the frame codec + write path converge in #37.3).  EBUSY detection
  moved from errno to g_error_matches(G_IO_ERROR_BUSY); the busy banner /
  auto-revert behaviour is unchanged.  GOTCHA settled: flock lives in
  pn_mesh_serial_open(), NOT open_configured() -- reopen() opens the new fd
  while the old still holds the lock, and two fds on one file conflict even
  within a process, so a flock in the shared helper would make every
  set_channel flash-commit bounce fail with EWOULDBLOCK.  Behaviour pinned by
  the #37.1 net: test-pn-mesh-node's 3 serial-open cases were repointed at
  pn_mesh_serial_open (exclusive case now asserts G_IO_ERROR_BUSY via flock,
  since pn_mesh_tty_in_use skips our own pid); all 84 unit tests pass.

  37.3 DONE Share discovery + framing.  The node's second frame-magic codec
  is gone: frame_wrap()/frame_extract()/PnFrameFn + PN_MESH_FRAME_SYNC1/2 +
  PN_MESH_FRAME_MAX deleted.  TX now builds a bare ToRadio PAYLOAD
  (build_text/want_config/heartbeat_payload) and pn_mesh_serial_write_frame()
  adds the 0x94 0xC3 + BE-len envelope; RX re-frames through
  PnMeshFrameReader (run_handshake + worker_main feed it and drain take()).
  serial_write_all() deleted too -- the shared open is blocking (it clears
  O_NONBLOCK after termios), so write_frame's EINTR-loop is the correct
  writer; the node's old EAGAIN/poll/deadline writer was only needed for its
  own non-blocking fd.  run_handshake() now takes PnMeshSerial* (writes via
  the shared writer, still reads the raw fd so worker_main can keep
  multiplexing it against the wake pipe in one poll()).  Discovery: the
  node's sysfs walk + its copy of the VID:PID table (known_devices,
  sysfs_read_id, find_tty_under) deleted; pn_meshtastic_list_devices()
  delegates to pn_mesh_discover_sync() and flattens the rich rows to the
  historical sorted/NUL-terminated tty strv -- ONE table (discover's
  KNOWN_DEVICES) is now the single home for #33's bare-CP2102 and #36's
  MM-ignore work.  DELIBERATE reconciliation of the #37.1 divergence: a
  zero-length frame is now YIELDED (the reader's behaviour) instead of the
  node's old skip -- harmless, the per-frame parsers no-op on len==0.
  Characterization net repointed: test-pn-mesh-node drops the frame_wrap/
  frame_extract cases (RX framing lives in test-pn-mesh-frame) and the
  find_tty/known_devices cases, gains write_frame_envelope (pty round-trip
  pinning the on-wire envelope) and payload-only build_*_payload byte
  vectors; NEW test-pn-mesh-discover compiles pn-mesh-discover.c directly to
  pin KNOWN_DEVICES / match_known_device / find_tty_device (one-level +
  nested + non-interface) that the node test used to cover.  Full suite green
  (0 failed); clean top-level build.

  37.4 Verify parity (node messaging + dialog config both still work, headless
  and GUI) then remove the dead duplicates.  [The headless half is covered by
